  "nl_text": "The database schema named \"schemabench_0081\" consists of four tables: 'personal_access_tokens', 'team_user', 'teams', and 'users'.\nThe 'personal_access_tokens' table is used to store personal access tokens, which are used for API authentication. It has columns for 'id', 'tokenable_type', 'tokenable_id', 'name', 'token', 'abilities', 'last_used_at', 'created_at', and 'updated_at'. The 'tokenable_id' column is a foreign key referencing the 'users' table.\nThe 'team_user' table is used to manage user-team relationships. It has columns for 'id', 'team_id', 'user_id', 'role', 'created_at', and 'updated_at'. The 'user_id' and 'team_id' columns are foreign keys referencing the 'users' and 'teams' tables respectively.\nThe 'teams' table is used to store team information. It has columns for 'id', 'user_id', 'name', 'personal_team', 'created_at', and 'updated_at'. The 'user_id' column is a foreign key referencing the 'users' table.\nFinally, the 'users' table is used to store user information. It has columns for 'id', 'name', 'email', 'email_verified_at', 'password', 'two_factor_secret', 'two_factor_recovery_codes', 'remember_token', 'current_team_id', 'profile_photo_path', 'created_at', and 'updated_at'. The 'current_team_id' column is a foreign key referencing the 'teams' table.\nAll columns allow null values except for 'abilities', 'two_factor_secret', and 'two_factor_recovery_codes'. Default values are not set for any of these columns. Primary keys are 'id' in all tables, and there are composite or unique constraints in 'personal_access_tokens' and 'team_user' tables. The 'users' table has a foreign key constraint on 'current_team_id' which references 'teams' table. The update and delete rules are not specified for any foreign key constraints.",
  "gold_question": "1. Background / Context\n\nLaravel Jetstream is an application starter kit for Laravel 8, designed to quickly scaffold new applications with aesthetically pleasing frontend interfaces using Tailwind CSS. It provides a robust foundation for building modern applications by integrating essential features such as authentication, session management, and API support.\n\n 2. Objectives\n\nThe primary objective of Laravel Jetstream is to offer developers a convenient starting point for Laravel applications with pre-built features, ensuring a streamlined development process. By utilizing either Livewire or Inertia.js for frontend scaffolding, Jetstream aims to boost productivity and maintain flexibility in application development.\n\n 3. Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Developers: Primary users who will use Jetstream to kickstart Laravel application development.\n- End Users: Indirect beneficiaries who will interact with applications developed using Jetstream.\n- Administrators: Users managing team settings and application configurations.\n\n 4. Functional Descriptions\n\n- Authentication: Provides user login, registration, and email verification.\n- Two-Factor Authentication: Ensures enhanced security for user accounts.\n- Session Management: Manages user sessions efficiently across devices.\n- API Support: Facilitated by Laravel Sanctum for easy integration and management of APIs.\n- Team Management: Optional functionality allowing users to collaborate as teams.\n- Frontend Options: Choice between Livewire and Inertia.js for interacting with the application.\n\n 5. Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Design and Usability: Utilizes Tailwind CSS to ensure a consistent and visually appealing user interface.\n- Performance: Optimized to handle common application requirements efficiently.\n- Scalability: Facilitates smooth scaling of applications as user demands grow.\n- Security: Integrates secure authentication processes and token management.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_deepseek/0081.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0081\nCREATE TABLE `personal_access_tokens` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `tokenable_type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `tokenable_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `token` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `abilities` text NOT NULL,\n  `last_used_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `tokenable_type_tokenable_id_unique` (`tokenable_type`, `tokenable_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `personal_access_tokens_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`tokenable_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `team_user` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `team_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `user_team_unique` (`user_id`, `team_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `team_user_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `team_user_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`team_id`) REFERENCES `teams` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `teams` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `personal_team` tinyint(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `teams_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email_verified_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `two_factor_secret` text NOT NULL,\n  `two_factor_recovery_codes` text NOT NULL,\n  `remember_token` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `current_team_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `profile_photo_path` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `users_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`current_team_id`) REFERENCES `teams` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
